<problem>
<!-- <title>Review derivative of exponential to introduce differential equations, 2</title> -->

<setup>

<function name="f" variables="t">3e^(7t)</function>
<function name="g" variables="t">-2e^(7t)</function>
<function name="h" variables="t">7e^(7t)</function>
<math name="fprime" simplify="full"><derivative>$f</derivative></math>
<math name="gprime" simplify="full"><derivative>$g</derivative></math>
<math name="hprime" simplify="full"><derivative>$h</derivative></math>
<math name="z" simplify="full">11e^(7t)</math>


</setup>


<p>Consider the functions <m>f(t)=<math extend="$f.formula" /></m>, <m>g(t)=<math extend="$g.formula" /></m>, and <m>h(t)=<math extend="$h.formula" /></m>.</p>



<!--Problem#1**********************************************-->
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Calculate the derivatives of <m>f</m>, <m>g</m>, and <m>h</m>.</p>

<!--<p style="line&#x2D;height: 250%">-->
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{ df }{ dt } =</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$fprime </award>
</answer></p>

<p>
<m>\displaystyle \frac{ dg }{ dt } =</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$gprime </award>
</answer></p>

<p>
<m>\displaystyle \frac{ dh }{ dt } =</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$hprime </award>
</answer>
</p>
</exercise>

<!--Problem#2********************************************-->
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>The expressions for those derivatives should be equal to the same thing as the function itself, multiplied by a number.</p>

<!--<p style="line&#x2D;height: 250%">-->
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{ df }{ dt } =</m> 
<answer>
<award>7</award>
</answer>
 <m>\times f(t)</m>
</p>

<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{ dg }{ dt } =</m> 
<answer>
<award>7</award>
</answer>
 <m>\times g(t)</m>
</p>

  
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{ dh }{ dt } =</m> 
<answer>
<award>7</award>
</answer>
 <m>\times h(t)</m></p>
</exercise>

<!--Problem#3*******************************************-->  
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>The function <m>v(t)</m> is one of those three function and is the solution to the differential equation <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dv }{ dt } = 7v(t)</m>.  Can you determine whether <m>v(t)=<math extend="$f.formula" /></m>,  <m>v(t)=<math extend="$g.formula" /></m>, or <m>v(t)=<math extend="$h.formula" /></m>?  
<answer inline="true">
<choiceInput>
<choice credit="1">no</choice>
<choice>yes</choice>
<choice credit="0.5">I'm clueless</choice>
</choiceInput>
</answer>
  Which of these are possibilities for the solution <m>v(t)</m>? 
<answer inline="true">
<choiceInput>
<choice credit="1">any of them</choice>
<choice>none of them</choice>
<choice>the first one</choice>
<choice>the second one</choice>
<choice>the third one</choice>
</choiceInput>
</answer>
</p>

<hint>
<p>If <m>v(t)</m> were equal to <m><math extend="$f.formula" /></m>, is it true that <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dv }{ dt }</m> is the same thing as <m>7v(t)</m>?</p>

<p>
If <m>v(t)</m> were equal to <m><math extend="$g.formula" /></m>, is it true that <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dv }{ dt }</m> is the same thing as <m>7v(t)</m>?
</p>

<p>
If <m>v(t)</m> were equal to <m><math extend="$h.formula" /></m>, is it true that <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dv }{ dt }</m> is the same thing as <m>7v(t)</m>?</p>

<p>Any function <m>v(t)</m> where <m>\frac{ dv }{ dt }</m> is the same thing as <m>7v(t)</m> is a possible solution, as it obeys the differential equation <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dv }{ dt }=7v(t)</m>.</p></hint>

</exercise>

<!--Problem#4*********************************************-->
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>If you were given the additional piece of information that <m>v(0)=3</m>, could you determine the identity of <m>v(t)</m>?  
<answer inline="true">
<choiceInput>
<choice credit="1">yes</choice>
<choice>no</choice>
<choice credit="0.5">I'm clueless</choice>
</choiceInput>
</answer>
 If so, what is <m>v(t)</m>?  <m>v(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$f </award>
</answer>
</p>
  
<hint>
If you have a number of possibilities for <m>v(t)</m>, does the requirement that <m>v(0)=3</m> narrow down the possible options?  For which of the listed options is <m>v(0)=3</m>?
</hint>

</exercise>

<!--Problem#5********************************************--> 
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>The function <m>w(t)</m> is one of those three functions and is the solution to the differential equation <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dw }{ dt } = 7w</m> with initial condition <m>w(0)=-2</m>.  What is <m>w(t)</m>?  </p>
<p><m>w(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$g </award>
</answer></p>

<hint>
The differential equation 
<me>\displaystyle \frac{ dw }{ dt }=7w</me>
is the same thing as 
<me>\displaystyle \frac{ dw }{ dt } = 7w(t).</me>
Some times we drop the argument <m>t</m>, and write <m>w(t)</m> as just <m>w</m> for brevity.
</hint>

</exercise>

<!--Problem#6********************************************-->
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Actually, we can solve this differential equation even if the answer is not one of those options.  If <m>z(t)</m> is a function that satisfies the differential equation <m>\frac{ dz }{ dt }=7z</m> with initial condition <m>z(0)=11</m>, what is <m>z(t)</m>?  </p>
<p><m>z(t)=</m>
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$z </award>
</answer></p>

<hint>
The answer is similar the other parts, with the only difference being the 11.
</hint>

</exercise>



<solution>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>\displaystyle \frac{ df }{ dt } = $fprime </m>, <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dg }{ dt }=$gprime </m>, <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dh }{ dt }=$hprime </m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>\displaystyle \frac{ df }{ dt }=7f(t)</m>, <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dg }{ dt }=7g(t)</m>, <m>\displaystyle \frac{ dh }{ dt }=7h(t)</m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
For all three functions, the derivative is equal to 7 times the function itself.  You could not determine which of those functions was <m>v(t)</m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
Yes, then you can conclude that <m>v(t)=<math extend="$f.formula" /></m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>w(t)=<math extend="$g.formula" /></m></p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>z(t)=z</m>.</p>
</exercise>

</solution>


</problem>